================================ 
Kubernetes Essentials — Quick Notes
================================ 

When working with Kubernetes, understanding the core building blocks makes everything easier.

1. Namespace
Used to logically isolate and organize resources within a cluster.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
   name: project_name
   labels:
      environment: dev
      project: project_name


2. Pod
Smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.

Key components inside a pod:
• env : Environment variables are key–value pairs passed into the container.
env:
 - name: APP_ENV
  value: "dev"


• labels : Labels are tags that you attach to pods.
labels:
 app: mysql
environment: dev
 tier: db

• annotations: Annotations are notes or metadata about your pod.

annotations:
 description: "This pod runs the cart service"


• configMap: ConfigMap stores non-sensitive configuration.
Example:
ConfigiMap Block:
name: app-config
data:
  APP_COLOR: "blue"

Pod Block:
envFrom:
  - configMapRef:
      name: app-config


• secret: Secret stores sensitive data (passwords)
Example:
stringData:
  DB_PASSWORD: "*********"
Pod consumes it like:

env:
  - name: DB_PASSWORD
    valueFrom:
      secretKeyRef:
        name: db-secret
        key: DB_PASSWORD

• resources: Defines CPU and memory requested & limited for your pod.
resources:
 requests:
  cpu: "100m" # m = millicores (1/1000 of a CPU core) i.e 0.1core
  memory: "128Mi" # (128 × 1,048,576 = 134,217,728 bytes)
 limits:
  cpu: "500m"
  memory: "512Mi"


3. Services:

• ClusterIP → Exposes the pod within the cluster. Enables pod-to-pod communication and internal load balancing using DNS.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
name : user
namespace: project_name
spec:
selector:
project: project_name
component: user
tier: backend
ports:
- protocol: TCP
port: 8080 # servcie port
targetPort: 8080 # container


• NodePort / LoadBalancer → Exposes the application to the outside world.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
   name: frontend
   namespace: project_name
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    project: project_name
    component: frontend
    tier: frontend
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80  # servcie port
      targetPort: 80 # container  


➡️ Pods use labels as selectors for services.

4. ReplicaSet
Ensures the desired number of pod replicas are always running.
spec:
    replicas: 1 # if give 2 here , 2 pods will be created for frontend micro service(container). 
    selector:
       matchLabels:
        project: project_name
        component: frontend
        tier: frontend

5. Deployment
Handles application deployment using images and performs rolling updates by default.
Ex:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
 name: frontend
spec:
 replicas: 2
 selector:
  matchLabels: { app: frontend }
 template:
  metadata: { labels: { app: frontend } }
  spec:
   containers: 
📌 Flow: Pod < ReplicaSet < Deployment
